## Payment API Tests
# Make sure Spring Boot is running on port 8080.
# Replace reservationId=1 with an existing reservation ID if needed.

### 1. Create a pending payment
POST http://localhost:8080/api/payments?reservationId=1&paymentMethod=Credit_Card
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Get payment by ID
# Replace YOUR_PAYMENT_ID with the paymentId returned from request 1.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/payments/YOUR_PAYMENT_ID
Accept: application/json

###

### 3. Mark payment as paid
# Replace YOUR_PAYMENT_ID with the paymentId from request 1.
# Replace 50000.00 with the exact amount returned by request 1.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/payments/YOUR_PAYMENT_ID/paid?transactionId=TEST123&paidAmount=50000.00
Accept: application/json

###

### 4. Mark payment as failed
# Replace YOUR_PAYMENT_ID with a PENDING payment ID.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/payments/YOUR_PAYMENT_ID/failed
Accept: application/json

###

### Cancellation API Tests

### 5. Create cancellation request
# Replace reservationId=1 with an existing reservation ID.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/cancellations?reservationId=1&requestedBy=Guest&cancellationReason=Testing
Accept: application/json

###

### 6. Get cancellation
# Replace YOUR_CANCELLATION_ID with the ID returned from request 5.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/cancellations/YOUR_CANCELLATION_ID
Accept: application/json

###

### 7. Approve cancellation
POST http://localhost:8080/api/cancellations/YOUR_CANCELLATION_ID/approve
Accept: application/json

###

### 8. Reject cancellation
POST http://localhost:8080/api/cancellations/YOUR_CANCELLATION_ID/reject
Accept: application/json

###

### Refund API Tests

### 9. Create refund
# Requires a PAID payment and an APPROVED cancellation.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/refunds?paymentId=YOUR_PAYMENT_ID&cancellationId=YOUR_CANCELLATION_ID
Accept: application/json

###

### 10. Get refund
GET http://localhost:8080/api/refunds/YOUR_REFUND_ID
Accept: application/json

###

### 11. Approve refund
POST http://localhost:8080/api/refunds/YOUR_REFUND_ID/approve
Accept: application/json

###

### 12. Mark refund as refunded
POST http://localhost:8080/api/refunds/YOUR_REFUND_ID/refunded
Accept: application/json

###

### 13. Reject refund
POST http://localhost:8080/api/refunds/YOUR_REFUND_ID/reject
Accept: application/json

###

### Invoice API Tests

### 14. Create invoice
# Normally the invoice is automatically created when a payment becomes PAID.
# Use this only if an invoice does not already exist for the payment.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/invoices?paymentId=YOUR_PAYMENT_ID
Accept: application/json

###

### 15. Get invoice
GET http://localhost:8080/api/invoices/YOUR_INVOICE_ID
Accept: application/json

###

### 16. Mark invoice as sent
POST http://localhost:8080/api/invoices/YOUR_INVOICE_ID/sent
Accept: application/json
